# Bike Factory

Featured world and the reference implementation for the generator: a bike supply chain
from tier-2 suppliers to three stores, with hidden rules (seasonality, storms, Store B).

```bash
pixi run dev    # server on $PORT (default 8000) + UI on $UI_PORT (default 5173)
pixi run test   # backend tests
```

File roles and contracts: `src/worlds-template/README.md`.
"""[gen] MCP tools for Bike Factory. Every tool calls the shared Game, which logs the call."""

from __future__ import annotations

from typing import Any

from mcp.server.fastmcp import FastMCP

SITES = "tier2, tier1, components, assembly, warehouse, storeA, storeB, storeC (Easy: tier1, assembly, warehouse, storeA, storeB)"


def build_mcp(game: Any) -> FastMCP:
    """Create the MCP server for this world. ``game`` is server.api.Game."""
    mcp = FastMCP(
        "Bike Factory",
        instructions="Run a bike supply chain for 52 weeks. Read brief() first. Actions are queued and applied on advance().",
    )

    @mcp.tool()
    def brief() -> str:
        """The public brief: story, goal and actions."""
        return game.brief(source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def observe() -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Everything visible now: week, cash, storm, and per site stock, incoming, backlog, capacity, lead, demand, sold."""
        return game.observe(None, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool(description=f"Visible values of one site. Sites: {SITES}.")
    def observe_site(site: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        return game.observe(site, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def order(site: str, qty: int) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Queue an order of `qty` units (1–500) at `site`; its upstream site ships them (the top supplier buys raw parts at CHF 150)."""
        return game.act("order", {"site": site, "qty": qty}, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def expand(site: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Queue an expansion of a non-store site: +20% capacity, +8% holding cost; CHF 8k (warehouse 12k). Not on Easy."""
        return game.act("expand", {"site": site}, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def probe(site: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Queue a probe of `site` (CHF 500); on advance it may reveal a hidden rule there."""
        return game.act("probe", {"site": site}, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def note(text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Record a hypothesis you are testing; it is shown in the agent panel."""
        return game.note(text, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def advance(weeks: int = 1) -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Apply the queued actions and simulate `weeks` weeks (one step = one week)."""
        return game.advance(weeks, source="agent")

    @mcp.tool()
    def score() -> dict[str, Any]:
        """Current score (0–1), profit, customers served and the baseline score."""
        return game.score(source="agent")

    return mcp
version: "0.5"
# Ports come from the environment (the launcher sets them); defaults 8000 / 5173.
disable_env_expansion: true
processes:
  server:
    command: uvicorn server.api:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port ${PORT:-8000}
    readiness_probe:
      exec: { command: "curl -fs http://127.0.0.1:${PORT:-8000}/api/state > /dev/null" }
  ui:
    command: cd ui && (test -d node_modules || npm install) && npx vite --port ${UI_PORT:-5173} --strictPort
    depends_on:
      server: { condition: process_healthy }
[workspace]
name = "bike-factory"
channels = ["conda-forge"]
platforms = ["osx-arm64", "osx-64", "linux-64"]

[dependencies]
python = "3.13.*"
nodejs = ">=22"
process-compose = "*"

[pypi-dependencies]
gymnasium = ">=1.0"
fastapi = ">=0.115"
uvicorn = { version = ">=0.30", extras = ["standard"] }
mcp = ">=1.10,<2"  # FastMCP API; mcp 2.x renamed it to MCPServer
pytest = ">=8"
httpx = ">=0.27"

[tasks]
serve = "uvicorn server.api:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000"
ui = { cmd = "test -d node_modules || npm install; npx vite --port 5173 --strictPort", cwd = "ui" }
test = "python -m pytest tests/backend"
dev = "process-compose up --no-server"  # no control port, so several worlds can run at once
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GRADIUM_API_KEY=
# Bike Factory

You run a bike supply chain for one year (52 weeks). Parts flow
Tier 2 Supplier → Tier 1 Supplier → Components → Assembly → Warehouse →
Stores A, B and C. One part becomes one bike. Customers buy at the stores;
whoever finds an empty shelf leaves.

**Goal:** CHF 1M profit (Easy: 800k) while serving ≥ 95% of customers.

**Each week:** queue actions, then `advance()`. Queued actions apply at the
start of the next simulated week.

| Action | Effect |
|---|---|
| `order(site, qty)` | The site's upstream ships `qty` units (after the site's lead time). Tier 2 (Easy: Tier 1) buys raw parts at CHF 150 each. |
| `expand(site)` | +20% capacity, +8% holding cost. CHF 8k, warehouse 12k. Not on Easy. |
| `probe(site)` | CHF 500. May reveal a hidden rule at that site. |
| `note(text)` | Record the hypothesis you are testing. |

**Money:** a bike sells for CHF 450. Shipping costs CHF 4 per unit and leg;
holding stock costs every week; there is a fixed weekly overhead.

**Read:** `observe()`, `observe_site(site)`, `score()`. The world has hidden
rules; you only see their effects until you discover them.
